1
00:00:00,370 --> 00:00:02,465
There are thousands
of grains.

2
00:00:02,505 --> 00:00:04,296
So why
not ‘many rice’?

3
00:00:04,837 --> 00:00:07,291
Zoom in and you
see grains.

4
00:00:07,331 --> 00:00:09,288
But when I say
rice as food,

5
00:00:09,328 --> 00:00:11,174
I mean the amount
in the bowl,

6
00:00:11,214 --> 00:00:12,867
not a list
of grains.

7
00:00:13,403 --> 00:00:13,804
So:

8
00:00:13,844 --> 00:00:15,818
‘I ate too much
rice for lunch.’

9
00:00:15,858 --> 00:00:17,449
Not ‘too many rice’.

10
00:00:18,370 --> 00:00:19,328
Want to count?

11
00:00:19,368 --> 00:00:20,488
Choose a unit:

12
00:00:20,528 --> 00:00:21,877
‘many grains
of rice’,

13
00:00:21,917 --> 00:00:23,560
‘two bowls of rice’.

14
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:26,256
The number goes onto
grains or bowls.

15
00:00:27,003 --> 00:00:28,552
Bread works
the same way:

16
00:00:28,592 --> 00:00:30,394
‘three slices
of bread’.

17
00:00:30,434 --> 00:00:31,532
Picture the amount,

18
00:00:31,572 --> 00:00:33,065
then pick the unit.

